    "According to you, how can LLMs be used to innovate math learning in schools and universities?": "LLMs could personalize learning by adapting explanations to a student’s level and pace, making abstract concepts more accessible. They could also provide instant feedback on problem-solving, helping students like me who struggle with anxiety. Interactive exercises and real-world applications would make math feel less daunting and more engaging."
